{
  "name": "suspend",
  "description": "Allows, but does not force suspend of the power elements of the matching driver node and its dependents.",
  "examples": [
    "To suspend a node by moniker\n\n    $ driver suspend dev.sys.platform.example.example-device\n\nTo disambiguate colliding monikers\n\n    $ driver suspend dev.sys.example#0123456789abcdef\n    $ driver suspend dev.sys.example --disambiguator 0123456789abcdef"
  ],
  "flags": [
    {
      "kind": "Switch",
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--help",
      "short": null,
      "description": "display usage information",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": {
        "Option": {
          "arg_name": "disambiguator"
        }
      },
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--disambiguator",
      "short": null,
      "description": "16-character structural disambiguator (from `driver node list -v` or `driver node show`) to disambiguate colliding monikers.",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": "Switch",
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--select",
      "short": "s",
      "description": "if this exists, the user will be prompted for a component to select.",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "This does not force suspend: it only removes the system-wide power dependency\nkeeping the node (and the nodes bound beneath it) active while the system is\nawake (for example, from wake leases or execution/activity leases). If another\nentity holds a direct lease on the driver's power element (or another element\nthat depends on it), the driver will remain active and will not suspend. The\nnode must have a driver bound to it. `driver node list -v` and `driver node show`\nreport a node's moniker, disambiguator, and owner (which is a driver URL if a\ndriver is bound to it). When multiple nodes share a moniker, pass\n--disambiguator (or `<moniker>#<disambiguator>`) to disambiguate.\nThe suspend session remains active until the command is interrupted (e.g. with\nCtrl+C)."
  ],
  "commands": [],
  "positionals": [
    {
      "name": "moniker",
      "description": "component moniker of the node to be suspended (optionally `<moniker>#<disambiguator>`).",
      "optionality": "required",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "error_codes": [
    {
      "code": 1,
      "description": "Failed to connect to the driver development service"
    }
  ]
}